NAR Lifecycle

	The NAR lifecycle copies the default Maven lifecycle and adds native goals to its phases.
The table below shows the different phases of the NAR Lifecycle and the goals (including
standard maven goals) attached to them. The order is left to right, top to bottom.

*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
| <Phase>                | <Goals (NAR Goals in bold)>                                         |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| validate               | <<nar-validate>>                                                    |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| initialize             | <<nar-download>>                                                    |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| generate-sources       | <<nar-unpack>>                                                      |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| process-sources        | <<nar-gnu-configure>>, <<nar-include-path>>                         |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| generate-resources     | <<nar-system-generate>>                             |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| process-resources      | resources, <<nar-resources>>, <<nar-gnu-resources>>                 |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| compile                | compile, <<nar-gnu-make>>, <<nar-compile>>           |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| process-classes        | <<nar-gnu-process>>, <<nar-process-libraries>>                      |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| generate-test-sources  | <<nar-test-unpack>>                                                 |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| process-test-sources   | <<nar-test-include-path>>                                           |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| generate-test-resources|                                                                     |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| process-test-resources | testResources                                                       |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| test-compile           | testCompile, <<nar-testCompile>>                                    |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| process-test-classes   |                                                                     |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| test                   | test, <<nar-test>>                                                  |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| prepare-package        | <<nar-prepare-package>>                                             |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| package                | <<nar-package>>, jar                                                |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| pre-integration-test   |                                                                     |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| integration-test       | integration-test                                                    |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| post-integration-test  |                                                                     |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| verify                 |                                                                     |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| install                | install                                                             |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 
| deploy                 | deploy                                                              |
*------------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+ 


	The NAR plugin attaches the nar files it produces to the main artifact (jar) so the standard
install and deploy plugins of maven do their job.

	The nar-assembly goal is not part of the lifestyle and should be called independently.

Include Path Goals: Pending Work

	The <<nar-include-path>> and <<nar-test-include-path>> goals publish the include
directories the sources compile against, so that an IDE can resolve the headers of a
project that <does not compile yet>. Two known limitations still get in the way of that
purpose, and both are pending:

	[[1]] <<The test goals run too late.>> <<nar-test-unpack>> is bound to
	generate-test-sources and <<nar-test-include-path>> to process-test-sources, and
	both of those phases come <after> compile in the standard lifecycle. There is
	therefore no way to obtain the include path of the test sources without compiling
	the module first, which is precisely what these goals exist to avoid. They should
	be rebound to phases before compile, as their main-scope counterparts already are
	(initialize, generate-sources and process-sources).

	[[2]] <<The goals are not self-sufficient on their own.>> They are meant to be
	callable from the command line (<<<mvn nar:nar-include-path>>>) even though they
	also run inside the lifecycle. They are invocable, but they collect the dependency
	include directories from the unpack directory and silently drop the ones that do
	not exist, so on a module that has just been cleaned they produce a
	c_cpp_properties.json holding only the project's own include directory, with no
	error or warning. To be genuinely standalone they must make sure the dependencies
	are resolved and unpacked themselves, instead of relying on earlier phases having
	run.

	[]

	Until both are addressed, a consumer of these goals has to drive them through the
lifecycle instead of calling them directly, and stop before compile. That is what the
Gjs Maven VS Code extension does: its Maven Update runs <<<mvn process-sources>>> on
C/C++ modules, and uses only target/nar/c_cpp_properties.json, leaving the test one
unused.
	
	
